          "guid": "mt2duefclhyfdoa3",
          "message": {
            "text": "The outline dropdown deliberately stays as-is — GB-1134's premise that it self-positions with bespoke inline styles is inaccurate for this popup.\n\nUnlike the theme context menu and language picker (body-appended, JS-positioned), this dropdown is appended to the sticky .outline-bar and positioned entirely by CSS: .outline-dropdown (0) is position: absolute; top: 100%; left: 0; right: 0 under the bar's positioning context. So it is already full-width-glued to its anchor and follows it on scroll with zero JS listeners — there is nothing to leak and no manual top/left math to replace.\n\nConverting it to autoReposition (body-append + fixed positioning) would regress it: it would lose the full-width match to the bar and add scroll/resize listeners for no gain. Left unchanged intentionally.",
            "markdown": "The outline dropdown deliberately stays as-is — GB-1134's premise that it self-positions with bespoke inline styles is inaccurate for this popup.\n\nUnlike the theme context menu and language picker (body-appended, JS-positioned), this dropdown is appended to the sticky `.outline-bar` and positioned entirely by CSS: [`.outline-dropdown`](0) is `position: absolute; top: 100%; left: 0; right: 0` under the bar's positioning context. So it is already full-width-glued to its anchor and follows it on scroll with zero JS listeners — there is nothing to leak and no manual top/left math to replace.\n\nConverting it to `autoReposition` (body-append + fixed positioning) would *regress* it: it would lose the full-width match to the bar and add scroll/resize listeners for no gain. Left unchanged intentionally."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/client/diff/outline.tsx"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 147,
                  "endLine": 174,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "function showDropdown() {\n  document.querySelectorAll('.outline-dropdown').forEach(el => { el.remove(); });\n\n  const bar = document.getElementById('outline-bar');\n  const symbols = symbolsSignal.value;\n  if (bar === null || symbols.length === 0) return;\n\n  const dropdown = toElement(\n    <div className=\"outline-dropdown\">\n      {renderSymbolList(symbols, 0)}\n    </div>\n  );\n\n  // Dropdown sits outside the breadcrumb mount tree (appended to `bar` after\n  // the mount-managed children), so a single delegated listener on the\n  // dropdown root is stable. Item clicks navigate + close.\n  void delegate(dropdown, 'click', '.outline-item', (_e, el) => {\n    const line = parseInt(asEl(el).dataset.line ?? '0', 10);\n    if (line > 0) {\n      scrollToLine(line);\n      dropdown.remove();\n    }\n  });\n\n  bar.appendChild(dropdown);\n\n  dismissOnOutsideClick(dropdown, undefined, () => [bar.querySelector('.outline-breadcrumb')]);\n}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
